---
<Base {...head}>
<section class="book-detail">
  <a class="back-link" href="/apps/">&larr; All apps</a>
  <div class="book-layout">
    <aside class="book-cover">
      <img src="/images/apps/simmer.png" width="512" height="512" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Simmer app icon — local recipe manager with AI imports for Android" style="border-radius: 28px;">
      <div class="book-meta">
        <div class="meta-row"><span>Status</span><span>Closed alpha</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span>Platform</span><span>Android</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span>Storage</span><span>Local-only · no account</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span>AI</span><span>BYOK · OpenAI · Gemini · Claude</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span>Pricing</span><span>Free · no ads · no subscription</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span>Publisher</span><span>Ink &amp; Iron Apps</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="buy-stack">
        <a class="btn btn-p" href="/contact.html?topic=alpha-simmer">Request alpha access</a>
      </div>
      <div class="author-contact">
        <span>App support</span>
        <a href="mailto:support@inknironapps.com">support@inknironapps.com</a>
      </div>
    </aside>
    <div class="book-body">
      <div class="kicker">App · Alpha</div>
      <h1>Simmer</h1>
      <p class="tagline"><em>Collect, modify, and shop from your recipes with AI-powered imports.</em></p>
      <div class="essay">
        <p>Simmer is a personal recipe manager built for people who actually cook. Collect recipes from anywhere, make them your own, and turn any meal plan into a smart shopping list — all without an account or the cloud.</p>
        <h3>Collect recipes from anywhere</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Type it in manually with a clean, distraction-free editor</li>
          <li>Paste a URL and Simmer fetches the recipe automatically using schema.org structured data — with an AI fallback for sites that don't play nicely</li>
          <li>Snap a photo of a recipe card, handwritten note, or cookbook page and let AI vision extract the details for you</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Make recipes your own</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Edit any recipe: adjust servings, swap ingredients, rewrite steps</li>
          <li>Add personal notes, ratings, and tags to keep your collection organized</li>
          <li>Track nutritional info, prep time, cook time, and difficulty</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Smart shopping lists</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Add any recipe to your shopping list in one tap</li>
          <li>Simmer merges duplicate ingredients automatically — no more "2 cups flour" appearing five times</li>
          <li>Check off items as you shop; the list updates in real time</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>AI that works your way</h3>
        <p>Simmer supports multiple AI providers so you choose what fits your setup:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>OpenAI (GPT-4o and later models)</li>
          <li>Google Gemini</li>
          <li>Anthropic Claude</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Bring your own API key — your key, your data, your cost.</p>
        <h3>Privacy first</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>No account required — open the app and start cooking</li>
          <li>All your recipes are stored locally on your device</li>
          <li>Nothing is sent to our servers; AI calls go directly from your device to your chosen provider</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Designed for daily use</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Clean dark and light themes that look great in any kitchen lighting</li>
          <li>Fast, fluid navigation built with Flutter</li>
          <li>Works offline — your recipes are always available, even without a connection</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Coming soon</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Share recipes with friends and family</li>
          <li>Community recipe discovery</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Whether you're recreating grandma's lasagna or experimenting with a new technique, Simmer keeps everything in one place — organized, editable, and ready to shop from. No subscription. No ads. No account. Just cooking.</p>
        <p>Currently in closed alpha. <a href="/contact.html?topic=alpha-simmer">request access via the contact form</a> if you want in.</p>
      </div>

      <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="simmer-faq-heading">
        <h2 id="simmer-faq-heading">Frequently asked</h2>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Simmer require an account?</summary>
          <p>No. Open the app and start cooking. There is no signup, no login, and no email collection.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where do my recipes live?</summary>
          <p>Locally on your device. Nothing is sent to Ink &amp; Iron Apps servers. AI calls, when used, go directly from your device to the AI provider you chose with your own API key.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which AI providers does Simmer support?</summary>
          <p>OpenAI (GPT-4o and later models), Google Gemini, and Anthropic Claude. You bring your own API key — your key, your data, your cost.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What does AI cost in Simmer?</summary>
          <p>Whatever your chosen provider charges. Simmer takes no markup and never proxies your calls. Most recipe imports use under a cent of tokens.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can Simmer import a recipe from a URL?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Simmer first tries structured-data extraction (Recipe schema.org markup that most modern recipe sites publish). For sites that don&rsquo;t have clean structured data, AI fallback handles the parse.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I import from a photo or handwritten note?</summary>
          <p>Yes — AI vision extracts ingredients, steps, and timing from photos of recipe cards, handwritten notes, or cookbook pages.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Simmer build shopping lists?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Add any recipe to your shopping list in one tap; Simmer merges duplicate ingredients automatically so &ldquo;2 cups flour&rdquo; doesn&rsquo;t appear five times. Check items off as you shop.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Simmer work offline?</summary>
          <p>Your recipes, edits, and shopping list all work offline. URL imports and AI features need internet — once a recipe is saved, it&rsquo;s available without a connection.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Simmer available on iOS?</summary>
          <p>Android only for the alpha. Simmer is built on Flutter so iOS is achievable later if there&rsquo;s demand.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I sign up to test Simmer?</summary>
          <p><a href="/contact.html?topic=alpha-simmer">Request access through the contact form.</a> Include your device, Android version, and which AI provider you&rsquo;d like to test with.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <aside class="related" aria-labelledby="simmer-related-heading">
        <h2 id="simmer-related-heading">More from the workshop</h2>
        <div class="related-list">
          <a class="related-card" href="/apps/libraryiq.html">
            <div class="related-kicker">Workshop · App</div>
            <div class="related-title">LibraryIQ</div>
          </a>
          <a class="related-card" href="/apps/matcalc.html">
            <div class="related-kicker">Workshop · App</div>
            <div class="related-title">MatCalc</div>
          </a>
          <a class="related-card" href="/books/">
            <div class="related-kicker">Library · By the maker</div>
            <div class="related-title">Books by Riley E. Antrobus</div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
